//! Entries slice — Batch 186 (Plan 181 / Research 218) — the ggml-cpu tiled
//! `mul_mat` k-quant distill: 9 `kernel_opt` rules (A x6, B x2, C x1),
//! distilled from `ggml-org/llama.cpp` commit
//! `d834d44e643681f7b046a22d357335f6f4ff6107` "ggml-cpu: tiled `mul_mat` for
//! k-quants" (#27851, jbooth, 2026-09-26) — 11 files ALL ggml-cpu + tests:
//! `iqp.cpp/.h` REMOVED (~1292 lines), a NEW `ggml-cpu/tiled/` kernel family
//! (~2175 lines: tiled.cpp + tiled-kernel.cpp + headers), ggml-cpu.c +48
//! restructure, and an 852-line test/bench harness. Commit's own numbers:
//! 3-6x for large matmul, break-even at 4096x64 * 64x4096, 80% (net loss)
//! for GEMV, quantization-class error only (max ~1e-4, rmse ~1e-5). This is
//! the CPU-lane twin of the prism-family kernel batches (B116 the FWHT
//! width ladder, B176 the #29096 dtype-native admission rule) — same
//! upstream, the ggml-CPU tier. The k-quants are NOT our scored `PQ2_0/PTQ1_0`
//! ternary class; what lands is the REGIME / admission / staging /
//! measurement substrate, never the architecture itself (a kernel port is
//! not a bounded fix-space — the six batch-parse gates exist precisely so
//! corpus rules stay mechanism-shaped).
//!
//! Source located IN the standing `../vendor/prismml-llama.cpp` (the M3/4090 vendor twin) clone
//! (the commit is upstream history the prism fork tracks); no fresh clone
//! consumed. Every load-bearing quote re-verified VERBATIM at the pin THIS
//! batch (Batch 31 discipline): `min_batch` tiled.cpp:1202-1205, the dead-tail
//! admission defect 615-642, narrow `k_extent` 664-679, `wdata_size` 651-658,
//! the ACTBIAS precompute 685-692, the maddubs overflow bound 216-226 +
//! 540-548, the NK=1/NK=0 dispatch 505-512, the VNNI interleave 568-576,
//! the jit band repack 543-546 + 815-822, zero-pad 541-562, chunk stepdown
//! 1096-1106, the force env 578-586, the consult site ggml-cpu.c:1269, the
//! MMID group 710-722 + per-expert floor 1230-1244, the owned F32->Q8_K
//! transform 1068-1082, the flush bench 343-357 + 441-443, the toggle
//! oracle 108-126 + 201-207, metadata widening tiled.cpp:36-56 + kernel
//! 125-133, the writeback transpose 684-696, and the removed iqp
//! late-consult comment (the `ggml-cpu.c` diff `-` lines).
